Subject: [candidate] do not release a borrowed file after close IRP allocation failure

Applies after 0009, 0012 and 0013. The CLOSE request owns the server file;
dispatch_close receives its borrowed zero-local-reference proxy and does not
acquire an Ob reference. An allocation failure must return STATUS_NO_MEMORY
without an unmatched dereference. Keep the zero-count invariant and the normal
request completion/ownership protocol. No token or access-path changes.

--- a/dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/ntoskrnl.c
+++ b/dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/ntoskrnl.c
@@ -677,8 +677,8 @@
     TRACE( "device %p file %p\n", device, file );
 
     if (!(irp = IoAllocateIrp( device->StackSize, FALSE )))
     {
-        ObDereferenceObject( file );
+        /* The server CLOSE request owns this borrowed file; no local ref was acquired. */
         return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
     }
 
